; EPM2 CO2 as a RIGID linear molecule built from virtual sites.
; Why: a flexible 180-degree angle plus two constrained C=O bonds is numerically
; unstable in GROMACS (LINCS failures on the CO2 bonds). Charges and LJ are EPM2
; (paper SI Table S1); bending is frozen, as in Part B (LAMMPS rigid CO2).
; Two massless-free dummies MW carry the whole mass (2 x 22.0049) at +-0.09797 nm,
; which reproduces the real moment of inertia; O1, C, O2 are virtual sites on the MW-MW axis.
[ moleculetype ]
CO2 2
[ atoms ]
;  nr type   resnr res  atom cgnr  charge    mass
   1  O_CO2  1    CO2  O1   1   -0.3256    0.0
   2  C_CO2  1    CO2  C    1    0.6512    0.0
   3  O_CO2  1    CO2  O2   1   -0.3256    0.0
   4  MW     1    CO2  MW1  1    0.0      22.0049
   5  MW     1    CO2  MW2  1    0.0      22.0049
[ constraints ]
   4  5  1  0.195949
[ virtual_sites2 ]
; site  from  to  funct  a      (x = (1-a) x_from + a x_to)
   1    4     5   1    -0.0863783
   2    4     5   1     0.5
   3    4     5   1     1.0863783
[ exclusions ]
1 2 3 4 5
2 1 3 4 5
3 1 2 4 5
4 1 2 3 5
5 1 2 3 4
